<p>Prints a timestamped entry to the log file.
</p>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Void%20keyword" title="Void keyword">void</a> PrintToLog(<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sMessage<br />);</div>
<dl>
<dt>Parameters:
<dd><dl><dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">sMessage<dd>The string entry to print to the log file.
</dl>
</dl><dl><dt>Returns:
<p><dd>Nothing.
</p>
</dl><dl><dt>Source:
<p><dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Script.ldf" title="Script.ldf">script.ldf</a>
</p>
</dl>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Prints an entry to the log file. Note this will only be visible if Script logging is enabled. To enable script logging open the <code>&lt;DragonAgeInstallDirectory&gt;\bin_ship\<a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/ECLog.ini" title="ECLog.ini">ECLog.ini</a></code> file and set <code>Script=1</code> in the <code>[LogTypes]</code> section. If this file doesn't exist, create it.
</p>
